<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iamblichus I of Emesa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 31 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iamblichus I was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Emesa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sampsigeramus-i">Sampsigeramus I</a>, who supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and other Roman commanders during the civil wars of the 40s and 30s BCE. Accused of treachery before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium">Battle of Actium</a>, he was executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> in 31 BCE. His son Iamblichus II was later restored to the throne by Augustus.</p></div>
